<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kondapalli</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kondapalli is a town near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayawada">Vijayawada</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, known for its hill fort and its brightly painted wooden toys. The fort was a stronghold of the Reddi kings in the 14th and 15th centuries and later passed through several dynasties before coming under the British. The Kondapalli toys, carved from a light local wood, are a recognised craft tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kondapalli.jpg" alt="Kondapalli" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Koushik · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kondapalli_killa_18.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
